Z||000012||Tryxalon||08-31-2001||08:42 PM||||Okay, I'm going to ask the question everyone should have asked: <P>Why do you want 140 horses out of the Duke? <P>Cam will move your power some, THe SD head will let it flow better, BUT <P>While the the Iron Duke is a durable, useful, and torque powerful economy-targeted engine, it does not respond well to hop-ups or to high rpms. <P>If you want to prove that you can travel in excess of legal speed limits and/or in excess of sanity ... you should probably look for an engine swap. It is also probably cheaper to swap one V-8 into it than to build up a 4 and then have to replace it as many have done.  <P>If you like "round town" torque, excellent handling, and good mileage, then the Duke is a good choice. <P>With a free flowing cat and muffler on the stock exhaust, Holley larger TBI, matching exaust and intake ports, and low restriction (K&N?) intake filter, The Duke has a nice amount of power for the car but it won't win a drag race with a Vette or a 5.0 Mustang.  It appears that anything beyond about 120hp is destined to disappoint.  <P>All that being said: I like my Iron Duke 4 banger. But then ....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> :lol <BR>  ||||reg||6
